    "details": {
      "alignment": "lawful neutral",
      "type": {
        "value": "humanoid",
        "subtype": "koopa"
      },
      "cr": 3,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<h1>Magikoopa — The Troop's Magical Backbone</h1><p>Magikoopas are the Koopa Troop's spellcasters—koopas who discovered magical aptitude and were trained in the traditions that Kamek established centuries ago. They wear blue robes, round spectacles that may or may not be prescription, and pointed hats that serve no magical function but have become traditional enough that going without one is considered professionally inappropriate. They ride broomsticks because Kamek rode a broomstick and tradition is tradition, though several younger Magikoopas have privately expressed interest in more modern transportation methods.</p><p>The Magikoopa magical tradition is distinct from the Mages' Guild's approach, from the Beanish magical systems, and from any other structured magical education in the region. Magikoopa magic is innate and species-specific—you either have the aptitude or you don't, and if you do, training refines it into a set of capabilities that includes shape-shifting objects, projectile energy blasts, and the teleportation that makes Magikoopas the Troop's most strategically mobile assets.</p><p>Standard Magikoopas serve as the Troop's magical support: healing wounded soldiers, enchanting equipment, providing magical reconnaissance, and—when combat requires it—delivering energy blasts that compensate for the Troop's otherwise limited ranged capability. They are not front-line combatants; their role is support and force multiplication, making other units more effective rather than winning engagements independently.</p><p>Kamek's return has energized the Magikoopa corps in ways that concern the Troop's non-magical personnel. The Magikoopas have always been loyal to Kamek before Bowser—he trained them, he established their traditions, he represents the magical heritage that gives their lives meaning. With Bowser absent and Kamek consolidating power, the Magikoopas' divided loyalty has become straightforward loyalty to Kamek, and their capabilities are being deployed according to Kamek's priorities rather than Bowser's standing orders.</p>",
        "public": "A robed koopa with round spectacles and a pointed hat, hovering on a broomstick with the dignified irritation of someone whose professional expertise is frequently undervalued by the non-magical soldiers they support."
      },
