  "items": [
    {
      "name": "Magical Blast",
      "type": "weapon",
      "img": "icons/magic/symbols/mask-yellow-orange.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>The Magikoopa's primary offensive spell: a shaped blast of magical energy that manifests as a geometric shape—typically a triangle, circle, or square—spinning toward the target with moderate speed and significant force. The shape is cosmetic rather than functional; all blast shapes deal the same damage. The variation exists because Kamek's original training manual included diagrams of different shapes and later generations of Magikoopas assumed each shape was a different spell rather than aesthetic options for the same effect.</p><p>The blast can be fired at a target within 60 feet as a ranged spell attack. On a hit, it deals 3d6 force damage. The damage type is force rather than elemental because Magikoopa magic operates on a fundamentally different principle than conventional arcane tradition—it manipulates reality directly rather than channeling elemental energies, which is why the blasts appear as abstract shapes rather than fire, ice, or lightning.</p>",
          "chat": "<p>A spinning geometric shape—today's shape is triangles—arcs toward the target with the professional precision of someone who has been doing this exact attack for their entire career.</p>"
        },
        "unidentified": {
          "name": "Geometric Energy Blast",
          "description": "<p>A ranged magical attack that manifests as spinning geometric shapes, dealing force damage through direct reality manipulation.</p>"
        },
