    {
      "name": "Shape-Shift Object",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/magic/control/buff-luck-fortune-green-gold.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>Magikoopas can transform non-magical, non-attended objects into different objects of similar size and mass. A brick becomes a coin. A barrel becomes a Goomba (temporary, reverts in 1 hour). A rock becomes a mushroom that may or may not be edible depending on the Magikoopa's skill with the particular transformation. The spell requires an action and affects one object within 30 feet that the Magikoopa can see.</p><p>The transformations are temporary—lasting 1 hour before reverting—but they're useful for creating improvised resources, confusing enemies, and the specific kind of battlefield modification that turns a corridor full of barrels into a corridor full of hostile Goombas while the enemy is navigating it. The Goombas created this way are real enough to fight, die, and headbonk with genuine commitment to their brief existences, which raises philosophical questions that Magikoopas prefer not to address.</p>",
          "chat": "<p>The barrel becomes a Goomba. The Goomba walks forward with the resigned determination of its species. In one hour, it will become a barrel again. It does not know this. It does not need to know this.</p>"
        },
