    {
      "name": "Healing Magic",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/magic/life/heart-glowing-red.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>Magikoopas can channel healing energy into wounded allies, restoring hit points through the same reality-manipulation magic that powers their offensive blasts. As an action, a Magikoopa can touch a creature and restore 2d8 + 3 hit points. This healing can be used three times per long rest, after which the Magikoopa's magical reserves need time to regenerate.</p><p>Healing magic is the primary reason Magikoopas are valued by the Troop beyond their combat capabilities. Koopa field medicine is otherwise limited to bandages and rest, and having magical healing available during prolonged engagements significantly reduces casualty rates. Magikoopas are instructed to prioritize healing over offensive action when casualties mount, a protocol that some Magikoopas resent (they trained for combat, not nursing) and others embrace (keeping soldiers alive feels more meaningful than adding to the body count).</p>",
          "chat": "<p>The wounds close under magical attention, reality being convinced that the damage didn't happen through the same principles that throw geometric shapes at enemies.</p>"
        },
