    {
      "name": "Broomstick Flight",
      "type": "equipment",
      "img": "icons/tools/hand/broom-straw-brown.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>Every Magikoopa rides a broomstick because Kamek rides a broomstick and tradition is tradition. The broomstick provides a fly speed of 30 feet with hover capability, allowing Magikoopas to maintain elevated positions during combat and traverse terrain that ground-bound forces cannot cross. The broomstick is not magical in itself—the flight is powered by the Magikoopa's innate magic channeled through the broom as a focusing implement.</p><p>If the broomstick is destroyed (AC 10, 5 HP), the Magikoopa loses flight capability until it can obtain a replacement. Any broom of appropriate size works as a replacement—the magic is in the rider, not the implement—though Magikoopas are oddly particular about bristle quality and handle finish, treating their brooms with the same care that soldiers treat their weapons.</p>",
          "chat": "<p>The broom shouldn't fly. The koopa on the broom makes it fly anyway. Tradition and magic combine to produce hovering koopas with geometric opinions about combat.</p>"
        },
        "unidentified": {
          "name": "Flight Broom",
          "description": "<p>A broomstick used as a magical flight implement. The magic is in the rider, not the broom, but the rider is particular about broom quality anyway.</p>"
        },
